%I A400852 #20 Oct 12 2026 12:13:59
%S A400852 8,10,12,2,8,23,10,12,18,8,3,8,20,2,23,10,16,10,8,15,8,4,0,8,53,2,20,
%T A400852 8,11,8,10,8,32,10,12,10,11,16,8,0,8,13,16,8,10,17,8,2,8,33,8,20,18,
%U A400852 15,8,8,38,2,12,10,8,4,8,12,10,8,43,2,8,11,8,20,0
%N A400852 Number of k such that the multiplicative group of squares modulo k is cyclic of order A396684(n).
%C A400852 Write Q(m) = {k : the multiplicative group of squares modulo k is cyclic of order m}, then Q(1) = {k : (Z/kZ)* = (C_2)^r} = {divisors of 24}; for m > 1, k is in Q(m) if and only if (Z/kZ)* is of the form (C_2)^r X C_{2m}.
%C A400852 Factor m = p_1*...*p_s > 1 into prime powers. Then numbers in Q(m) are of the form d*q_{S_1}*...*q_{S_t}, where S_1, ..., S_t is a partition of {1, 2, ..., s}, q_{S_i} is a prime power such that (Z/q_{S_i})* = C_{2*Product_{j in S_i} p_j} or C_2 X C_{2*Product_{j in S_i} p_j}, and d is a divisor of 24 coprime to q_{S_1}*...*q_{S_t}.
%C A400852 |Q(m)| is divisible by 4 for odd m: We have Q(m) = {k, 2*k, 4*k, 8*k : k odd in Q(m)}.
%C A400852 |Q(m)| is even for m not divisible by 3: We have Q(m) = {k, 3*k : k in Q(m) not divisible by 3}.
%C A400852 |Q(m)| is divisible by 8 if m is divisible neither by 2 nor by 3.
%H A400852 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400852/b400852.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A400852 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400852/a400852.txt">Examples showing the procedure to find Q(m)</a>.
%H A400852 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400852/a400852_1.txt">List of Q(m) for the first 10000 values of m in A396684</a>.
%H A400852 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400852/a400852_2.txt">PARI program for A400852</a>.
%H A400852 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiplicative_group_of_integers_modulo_n">Multiplicative group of integers modulo n</a>.
%e A400852 a(1) = 8 since there are 8 values for k such that the multiplicative group of squares modulo k is trivial, namely k = 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24.
%e A400852 a(2) = 10 since there are 10 values for k such that the multiplicative group of squares modulo k is cyclic of order 2, namely k = 5, 10, 15, 16, 20, 30, 40, 48, 60, 120.
%o A400852 (PARI) for(n=1, 200, if(is(2*n), print1(#multgp(n), ", "))) \\ See _Charles R Greathouse IV_'s second program in A002174 and the PARI program link for multgp
%Y A400852 Cf. A400860 (smallest member in Q(m)), A400853 (largest member in Q(m)), A400856 (m such that Q(m) is nonempty), A400857 (m such that Q(m) is empty).
%Y A400852 Cf. A396684.
%K A400852 nonn,new
%O A400852 1,1
%A A400852 _Jianing Song_, Oct 07 2026
